        "text": "I have created the following Python files in the current working directory:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] extract_text.py** - extracts plain text from a scanned document image using AWS Textract.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] extract_layout.py** - extracts blocks, lines, tables, or layout elements from a document using AWS Textract.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] extract_tables.py** - extracts table cells and row structure from a document using AWS Textract.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] extract_key_values.py** - extracts key-value pairs from a form-like document using AWS Textract.\n5. **[HELPER] document_client.py** - provides local configuration and client helper utilities for OCR and Layout Extraction.\n6. **[HELPER] document_models.py** - defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for OCR and Layout Extraction.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] ocr_translate.py** - translates extracted OCR text using AWS Translate.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] ocr_safety.py** - checks extracted document text for unsafe content using AWS Comprehend.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] document_field_extraction.py** - extracts structured fields from OCR-normalized document text using AWS Comprehend.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] ocr_embedding.py** - embeds extracted document sections for semantic retrieval using AWS Comprehend.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses AWS services and makes the provider identifiable in the code. The local helper files provide configuration and utility functions to support the main tasks.",
